Subject: Ask for the Wi-Fi password again after a wrong one

When a password-protected network fails to connect, NetworkManager keeps the
profile with the wrong password. Clicking the network again silently reuses
it and the password prompt never comes back. Forget the profile on failure
(except Enterprise networks), so the next click asks again.

Side effect: a saved network that fails for another reason (weak signal)
is forgotten too and needs its password again.

--- a/src/quickshell/network/NetworkPopup.qml	2026-11-13 14:59:16.255044373 +0700
+++ b/src/quickshell/network/NetworkPopup.qml	2026-11-13 14:59:16.259950096 +0700
@@ -323,6 +323,8 @@
                         if (network.name) delete bt[network.name];
                         window.busyTasks = Object.assign({}, bt);
                         window.connectingId = "";
+                        // Wrong password: forget the profile so the next click asks for the password again
+                        if (network && network.security > 0 && network.security !== 6 && !network.connected) network.forget();
                     }
                 }
             }
